    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0683" n="539" xml:id="pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/107: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-07T20:00:00-05:00">February 7, 1929—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Navy Department gives advance information that, subject to there being no
                    objection by the Department of State and subject to conditions in China, it
                    plans to withdraw from China waters the three light cruisers on April 25 and not
                    to replace them. Reply has been made that no objection is at present
                    perceived.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
